From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:41:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make the menus fit a handheld console

- Prompts ask for the A and B buttons instead of the Y and N keys, and
  yes/no prompts also accept Enter and Backspace, which the buttons send.
- New savegames are named after the level and time, eg. "E1M3 30/09
  14:05", and names can be edited with the d-pad: up and down cycle the
  last letter, right adds one, left removes one.
- Without writable storage, like a Nintendo DS without an SD card,
  saving ended the game with an I_Error. Save Game and Quick Save now
  check first and show a message, so you can keep playing.
- No Read This! (keyboard help), mouse sensitivity or sound volume
  menus: there is no keyboard or mouse, and the hardware volume control
  sets the loudness, so sound and music always play at full volume.
---
 doomgeneric/d_englsh.h |   4 +-
 doomgeneric/m_menu.c   | 118 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 100 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

